🟡 13. Terraform with Helm
🧠 What is Helm?

👉 Helm is a package manager for Kubernetes

It helps install and manage applications in Kubernetes using reusable charts

Examples:

nginx-ingress
metrics-server
prometheus
argocd

🔥 Terraform + Helm Together

👉 A common DevOps workflow is:

Terraform creates EKS cluster
Terraform or Helm deploys Kubernetes applications

👉 Terraform can manage Helm charts using the Helm provider

🔹 Simple Flow

Terraform -> creates cluster
Helm -> installs applications on cluster

🔥 Why Use Helm?

Easy installation of Kubernetes apps
Reusable chart-based deployment
Version control of app packages
Easy upgrades and rollback

🔥 Example Use Cases

Install ingress controller
Install monitoring stack
Install cert-manager
Install Argo CD

🔥 Terraform Helm Provider Concept

Terraform can define:

provider "helm" { ... }

and manage:

resource "helm_release" "nginx" { ... }

👉 This allows Helm deployments through Terraform workflow

⚠️ Best Practice

Use Terraform with Helm mainly for platform-level tools

Examples:

ingress controller
monitoring
logging
cluster add-ons

Avoid using Terraform Helm for every application release in very dynamic delivery pipelines

🔥 Interview Questions
❓ What is Helm?

👉
